<h2>How to read this standard</h2>
<h3>Severity</h3>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Severity</p></th><th><p>Meaning</p></th><th><p>Target fix time (align with policy)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Direct path to compromise or outage</p></td><td><p>e.g., 7 days</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Significant weakness in access, crypto or logging</p></td><td><p>e.g., 30 days</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Hardening gap with limited direct exposure</p></td><td><p>e.g., 90 days</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Grey</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">LOW</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Best practice or hygiene item</p></td><td><p>e.g., next change window</p></td></tr></tbody></table>
